<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28144" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοτ-ήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>giver, dispenser,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταμίαι . . σίτοιο δοτῆρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					19.44
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀϊστοὶ θανάτοιο δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			; esp. of the gods, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. εὐθηλέος ἥβης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					8.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαντευμάτων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>Pae.</u>
					7.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὸς βροτοῖς δοτῆρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					612
				</span></i>
			.—Poet. form used by <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.9
			</span></i>, and in later Prose, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεὸς δ. παντὸς ἀγαθοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.62
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				J.
				<u>AJ</u>
				1.18.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Iamb.
				<u>Myst.</u>
				3.31
			</span></i>.</div>
